Sval: a removed tab-scoped permission reaches every process holding a copy

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2064718 (mozilla-central a845ae2cf750, Firefox
156), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
PermissionManager::ForwardBrowserPermissionToChild sent a change to a
tab-scoped permission only to the process showing the tab. A page the tab
left keeps its process's copy, in the bfcache and in a later load there,
which TransmitBrowserPermissionsForPrincipal seeded, so a grant removed
after the tab moved to another process applied again on going back. A
removal reaches every process that NeedsPermissionsUpdate for the
permission's key. A clear of a tab's permissions reaches every process: it
names no origin, and on a tab's close GetCurrentTopByBrowserId no longer
finds the tab. Its test is browser_temporary_permissions_child_clear.js.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 156.

